  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activity under preparation Special Measures for Libya 2024 - Support to the Justice and Rule of Law Systems in Libya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This action builds on previous EU funded justice and rule of law support in Libya. It develops previously identified good practices and responds to the needs expressed by Libyan stakeholders.Because of the extended transition phase since the revolution and the fragile social contract between state and citizens, other actors such as armed groups have filled the vacuum, resulting in a hybrid and unreliable system of law, justice and accountability. In this context, the rule of law and access to justice are essential to reaching an inclusive social contract, fighting corruption, building peace and ensuring the equality and legitimacy of decision-making bodies. Support to the justice and rule of law systems are also key instruments of stabilisation, recovery and reconciliation across the whole of Libya. The Overall Objective of this action is to strengthen justice and rule of law in Libya. The action Specific Objective is to enhance access to reinforced and more inclusive justice and rule of law institutions.</narrative>
  </description>
